  "goodToKnow": "Schleusen means to pass a ship through a canal lock (die Schleuse) and, much more often in the news, to smuggle people across borders: Migranten über die Grenze schleusen. Der Schleuser is a people smuggler (also Schlepper), and die Schleuserbande a smuggling gang. Germany's Kiel Canal, with large locks at each end, is one of the world's busiest artificial waterways. Regular: schleuste, geschleust."
